	spec: 'SYSTEM.md encourages optional concise human-readable BASH purposes and purposes for complex EDITs only when interactive=true. Replace the former requirement that every BASH has a purpose comment. Explicit session and delivered human-message metadata determine mode, never spawn kind, ownership, autoclose or host terminal presence. New hal -p sessions are noninteractive, including --keep; print submits to existing sessions are noninteractive when delivered, while queued print messages leave the current mode unchanged. Later UI prompts restore interactive guidance. Spawned sessions and forks inherit the source mode. Mode changes rebuild the system prompt instead of retaining interactive syntax in its cached prefix. Unattended runs receive no built-in prompt, ordinary help/schema or error usage teaching purpose-comment syntax. Shared help and usage remain comment-free. Malformed supplied comments still receive accurate diagnostics; historical calls and user instructions are preserved, not rewritten to conceal previously supplied syntax. Parsing, optional descriptions, command arguments, validation, atomic edits and complete error visibility remain unchanged. Regression coverage exercises watched subagents, unattended prompt rendering, shared HELP and errors, print metadata, queued delivery and cached mode transitions.',
